### Additional Context

I found that the problem with this type 

```typescript
export type QueryDeepPartialEntity<T> = _QueryDeepPartialEntity<
    ObjectLiteral extends T ? unknown : T
>
```

When we pass a generic here, it's erasing the information about any types that it forces to extend, so it's deciding that my generic is an object literal, but it actually not.  

I think it makes sense to change it to this 

```typescript 

/**
 * Make all properties in T optional. Deep version.
 */
export type QueryDeepPartialEntity<T> = _QueryDeepPartialEntity<
    T extends "toString" ? T : unknown
>
```

I found a few other places where people distinguish between classes and objects so probably it makes sense to change it. 
But I need input from somebody who is more aware of the project. 

